<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">drink</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">drink</ansi> command drinks an item you carry (if it is drinkable).

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">drink potion</ansi>
  This would drink your potion.

<ansi fg="yellow">Good to know:</ansi>

  - If you wear a potion bandolier, <ansi fg="command">drink</ansi> draws from it first
    (oldest potion first), then from your backpack.
  - Potions age: a brew grows stronger as it ferments toward its
    peak, then declines. A spoiled potion will make you ill —
    <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> at it first if it has been sitting a while.
  - Potions carry toxicity. Drink too many too fast and the poison
    builds up in you; see <ansi fg="command">help toxicity</ansi>.
  - You cannot drink while grappled — both hands are committed.
    Drinking also waits while you are focused on crafting,
    salvaging, or casting.
  - If something else shares the name, <ansi fg="command">drink</ansi> reaches for the
    drinkable one.

Find out more about referring to items by name by typing <ansi fg="command">help item-names</ansi>.

